Golem AFK
=========

Keeps Minecraft accounts online on a server while this app is open.

Start
  Double-click "Start Golem AFK.bat". A black window opens (keep it open)
  and the dashboard opens in your browser at http://localhost:8080.
  The first time, pick a dashboard password.

Add a bot
  Click "Add bot", enter the server, and press "Add and start".
  For a Microsoft account you'll see a code: open microsoft.com/link,
  enter it and sign in with that account. You only do this once.

From your phone
  Same Wi-Fi as this PC: open the address shown in the black window
  (http://192.168.x.x:8080). If Windows asks about the firewall,
  allow Node.js on private networks.

Run without the black window
  Settings > "Start Golem AFK in the background when Windows starts".
  Quit it from Settings > "Quit Golem AFK".

Updating
  Settings > Updates > "Install update from a zip" and pick the new
  Golem AFK.zip. Only changed files are replaced; your bots, password
  and Microsoft sign-ins stay. The app restarts by itself.

Your data
  Everything (password, bots, saved sign-ins, chat logs) is kept in the
  "data" folder next to this file. Delete the whole folder to remove the app.

Is it allowed?
  That depends on each server's rules. Use alt accounts where unsure.

